<article class="env-definition" id="00JX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00JX">Definition <span data-tag="00JX">10.58.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be an abelian group. We say that a function $f : n \mapsto f(n) \in A$ defined for all sufficient large integers $n$ is a <em>numerical polynomial</em> if there exists $r \geq 0$, elements $a_0, \ldots , a_ r\in A$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f(n) = \sum \nolimits _{i = 0}^ r \binom {n}{i} a_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $n \gg 0$. </p>
</article>